and applications through a centralized dashboard; and data protection as-a-service solutions, such as backup and disaster recovery for servers, virtual machines, workstations, files, data, and key cloud-based applications, as well as multi-tenant platform and secure remote delivery architecture. Further, it offers security services through endpoint security, managed detection and response, extended detection and response, web protection, e-mail security, and archiving solutions. Additionally, the company engages in the professional services automation, automation and scripting management, password management policies, and reporting and analytics activities. The company was incorporated in 2020 and is headquartered in Burlington, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John  Pagliuca | CEO, President & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $934,500 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $277K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, improving at 10%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $41K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $25K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["N-able, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $914M market cap on $511M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 84% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $75M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 15 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Goodwill represents 73% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 79/100): structural revenue/margin decline; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Technology peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Gross margin tops the Technology peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"N-able expects Q4 revenue of $133M-$134M while proj